@startuml SquadSyncAuthSequence

title SquadSync Login and Identity Cookie Sequence

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30
skinparam BoxPadding 15
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC

actor Browser
participant "Cloudflare Edge" as Cloudflare
participant "cloudflared Tunnel" as Tunnel
participant "Kubernetes Ingress" as Ingress
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Auth Service" as Auth
participant "Identity Service" as Identity
participant "Google OAuth" as Google
database "PostgreSQL" as Postgres
participant "Squad Service" as Squad

== Login ==

alt Password login
  Browser -> Cloudflare : POST /api/auth/login\nemail + password
else Google login
  Browser -> Google : Sign in with Google
  Google --> Browser : Google ID token credential
  Browser -> Cloudflare : POST /api/auth/google\ncredential
end

Cloudflare -> Tunnel : Forward HTTPS request
Tunnel -> Ingress : Route request
Ingress -> Gateway : /api/auth/*
Gateway -> Auth : Login request

alt Password credential
  Auth -> Postgres : Find user and verify password
  Postgres --> Auth : User record
else Google credential
  Auth -> Google : Verify ID token
  Google --> Auth : Verified subject and email
  Auth -> Postgres : Find or create linked user
  Postgres --> Auth : User record
end

Auth -> Identity : Planned internal token request
Identity -> Identity : Sign JWT with private key
Identity --> Auth : Signed JWT

Auth --> Gateway : Set-Cookie: squadsync-access
Gateway --> Ingress : Forward Set-Cookie
Ingress --> Tunnel : HTTPS response
Tunnel --> Cloudflare : Tunnel response
Cloudflare --> Browser : Set-Cookie response
note right of Browser
  Browser stores the JWT in an
  HttpOnly, Secure cookie.
  JavaScript does not read it.
end note

== Authenticated API request ==

Browser -> Cloudflare : GET /api/squads\nCookie: squadsync-access
Cloudflare -> Tunnel : Forward HTTPS request
Tunnel -> Ingress : Route request
Ingress -> Gateway : /api/squads
Gateway -> Squad : Forward Cookie header
Squad -> Identity : Fetch JWKS public key
Identity --> Squad : Public verification key
Squad -> Postgres : Query squad_db with Pool
Postgres --> Squad : Squad data
Squad --> Gateway : 200 response
Gateway --> Ingress : Forward response
Ingress --> Tunnel : HTTPS response
Tunnel --> Cloudflare : Tunnel response
Cloudflare --> Browser : 200 response

note over Auth,Identity
  The Auth-to-Identity token exchange is the target design.
  The current scaffold has the pieces but does not wire this call yet.
end note

@enduml
